note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/nvidia/checks/arestg.om: the shared part of the arest checks that hold several units of one head (data,
note pack, tile, tern, bf16, pkh) or a unit of the packing(), prefill() and partition blocks of CUDApp
note tests/api_rest_diff.c and tests/api_rest_partitions.h. A check is the units' parts (gpu/units.tsv), lib.om,
note lib-om2.om, its arest-CHECK.om (text t_name, fn arop) and then this part. Rows:
note   UNIT NY Q E R
note UNIT names the call; arop reads it (ckis 0) and gives the unit the Q words in its own layout. Q is at most 256
note words of 16 hex digits (- for none); NY is the length of the unit's output view where the row sets it. E lists
note (index, value) word pairs: index i below 128 is output word i, index 128 + p is input word p of Q after the
note call (the views a unit edits). R is the unit's answer, one word, last so that the gate's table control changes
note a word. Where the old test fills a large array by a loop, Q holds the loop's parameters, arop ports the loop and
note output word 0 is the digest of the unit's output (ardg), which the table holds for the old test's expectation.
fn cname to void
for i ulong len t_name bound 64
ckoc ulong get t_name i
end
end
note word j of field i, a run of 16 hex digits
fn arw i ulong j ulong to ulong
w = ulong 0
for k ulong 8
w = or shl w 8 ckhex i add mul j 8 k
end
ret w
end
note the digest: FNV-1a over whole elements, from ardg0
fn ardg0 to ulong
ret 14695981039346656037
end
fn ardg h ulong v ulong to ulong
ret mul xor h v 1099511628211
end
fn crow to bool
if ne ckcnt 5
ckbad
end
ny = cknum 1
nb = ckhexn 2
eb = ckhexn 3
if or gt nb 2048 ne rem nb 8 0
ckbad
end
if ne rem eb 16 0
ckbad
end
if ne ckhexn 4 8
ckbad
end
nq = div nb 8
q = new ulong 256 0
for j ulong nq bound 256
put q j arw 2 j
end
o = new ulong 256 0
r = arop q nq ny o
if ne r arw 4 0
ret false
end
for j ulong div eb 16 bound 1099511627776
k = arw 3 mul j 2
if ge k 256
ckbad
end
if ne get o k arw 3 add mul j 2 1
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
